<tr>
<td><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Career Outlook</span></td>
<td>
<p>Students who study Business Administration may find themselves working as a Bookkeeper, Accountant, or an Auditing Clerk. These positions are considered to be an organization's financial record keepers and represent a variety&nbsp;of skills and knowledge. Salaries in California range from $34,200 - $54,770. For more information&nbsp;on these careers, please refer to the <a title="California Occupational Guide- BSN" href="http://www.labormarketinfo.edd.ca.gov/occguides/Detail.aspx?Soccode=433031&amp;Geography=0604000017" target="_blank" rel="noopener">California Occupational Guide</a>.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><span style="font-size: 14pt;">Potential Salary with a Degree or Certificate: <a title="Salary Surfer" href="http://salarysurfer.cccco.edu/Salaries.aspx" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Salary Surfer</a></span></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Financial Aid &amp; Scholarships</span></td>
<td>
